From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8650: let the PCIe GDSCs power off in s2idle

Mainline keeps the SM8650 PCIe GDSCs in retention across gdsc_disable()
(PWRSTS_RET_ON). With the controller still powered on the PCIe NoC, the
s2idle wake needs a PCIe bus vote in the sleep set (0527), which keeps the
MC0 BCM voted and stops CX and DDR from collapsing.

armada-os/armada#723 found the same on SM8750: with the GDSCs allowed off
(0044 dropped) the WCN7860 Wi-Fi resumes fine and CXSD/DDR are entered.
Test on the TB321FU (WCN7850), together with 0527 dropped.
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c	2026-10-14 18:12:13.278183355 +0200
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c	2026-10-14 18:12:13.297714201 +0200
@@ -3436,7 +3436,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3447,7 +3447,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3458,7 +3458,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3469,7 +3469,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
